<title>BRAZIL: Brazil 1996 current account deficit 3.27 pct of GDP.</title>
<headline>Brazil 1996 current account deficit 3.27 pct of GDP.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil posted a current account deficit in 1996 of $24.347 billion, equivalent to 3.27 percent of Gross Domestic Product, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that the 1995 current account deficit was 2.47 percent of GDP.</p>
</text>
